WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.635
-Welcome back, everybody.
Today is Friday,

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.170
and that's usually when I catch
up with some personal stuff.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.238
I check my inbox,
return some emails,

00:00:06.238 --> 00:00:08.107
and of course send out
thank you notes.

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:09.508
And I was running
a bit behind today,

00:00:09.508 --> 00:00:10.910
so I thought,
if you guys wouldn't mind,

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.145
I'd like to write up my weekly
thank you notes right now.

00:00:13.145 --> 00:00:15.314
Is that cool with you?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:17.217
Appreciate it, thank you.

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:18.584
James, can I get some
thank-you-note

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.887
writing music, please?

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:25.892
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.092
-There's a few beans
in his cabinet.

00:00:27.092 --> 00:00:30.863
-Wow.
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:33.433
-Thank you, Mother's Day,
for being that special

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.435
time of year where kids
force their moms

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:38.404
to eat a mediocre breakfast
in an uncomfortable position.

00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:39.972
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:39.972 --> 00:00:42.842
Thank you.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.377
-Oh, I spilled it.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.912
-[ Chuckles ]

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.280
♪♪

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.916
Thank you,
photo of Joe and Jill Biden

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:52.952
visiting former President Carter
and his wife,

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.221
for looking like a
still from the upcoming movie

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.689
"Honey, I Shrunk the Carters."

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:58.591
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.959
[ Applause ]

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.561
-This is good.

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:10.203
-Thank you, first week of May,
for flying by so quickly.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.537
I mean, before you know it...

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:13.972
-♪ It's gonna be... ♪
-June.

00:01:13.972 --> 00:01:15.641
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:17.610
-Do you know this song?

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.712
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:27.086
Thank you, "Game of Thrones"
prequel "House of the Dragon"

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:29.255
for giving the Internet
something to be mad about

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.190
when the finale airs
in eight years.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:34.293
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:36.663
I didn't like it.
-I don't like it at all.

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:41.968
-Thank you, FDA for authorizing

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:44.871
the use of the Pfizer vaccine
for teenagers.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.806
Although if you really want to
get teenagers to get vaccinated,

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:48.775
just tell them
that they're not allowed.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:51.077
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:53.746
You can't tell me
what to do, dad.

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:56.249
-I'm going to clean up this
whole yard and my room, too.

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:57.650
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.719
I'll change the oil on the car.

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:01.787
-How old are you, son?

00:02:01.787 --> 00:02:03.155
-My son is 75.

00:02:03.155 --> 00:02:04.190
-Oh.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.859
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:08.695
-Thank you, Cicadas.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:10.630
This past year has been hard
on all of us,

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.732
so it's nice to know
a swarm of loud,

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.733
hideous bugs is about to arrive.

00:02:14.733 --> 00:02:17.137
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:26.346
Thank you, waiter pouring water,
for making me think do we stop

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:28.747
talking completely,
and suddenly watch him pour,

00:02:28.747 --> 00:02:32.385
carry on our conversation,
or fake talk until he leaves?

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.320
[ Applause ]

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.123
Thank you good.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.624
-We're good.

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:42.561
We're good.
-We're good.

00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:45.265
Thank you, baseballs,
for looking like you just

00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:47.099
got out of a major surgery.

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:49.335
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:57.877
Thank you, diners,
for being the only restaurant

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:00.746
where half the menu items
just sound like dares.

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:03.482
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:03.482 --> 00:03:07.253
Filet of cod with fresh fruit
and coleslaw?

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:08.721
-I'll take that.
-Sure, why not?

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:11.156
-Jell-O with marshmallows in it?
Alright.

00:03:11.156 --> 00:03:12.659
-Should I get the lobster?

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:14.193
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:15.328
-I'm going to get the fresh --

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:17.263
-I wouldn't get the lobster.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:18.597
-I have a choice.
-It's 3:00 in the morning,

00:03:18.597 --> 00:03:19.598
we just left the bar.

00:03:19.598 --> 00:03:21.500
-Are you sure?
-I'm just saying.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:22.568
I haven't been here before.
-It's either a patty melt

00:03:22.568 --> 00:03:24.036
pr lobster scampi.

00:03:24.036 --> 00:03:25.872
-I would -- I would just go
with a burger and fries

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:27.674
or something like that.
-Mm, I don't know.

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:31.010
I think I'll get the octopus,
and...

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.312
-Yeah.

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:36.015
-...the creme brulee.
-Ah.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.282
They make creme brulee
at this diner?

00:03:37.282 --> 00:03:40.186
-Oh, yeah.
This diner is fantastic.

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:41.687
It's Jell-O
that somebody burned.

00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:43.856
-Yeah, burned Jell-O.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:45.324
-More brulee than creme.

00:03:45.324 --> 00:03:47.360
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.661
-Something brulee.

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:51.130
-Yeah, and it's orange Jell-O.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.631
-I like orange Jell-O.
-I love orange Jell-O.

00:03:52.631 --> 00:03:54.467
Are you kidding me?
-Are you joking me?

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.235
-No, I love all kinds of Jell-O.
Are you talking me down?

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:58.270
I love orange Jell-O.
-I love every type of Jell-O.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.306
-Do you really?
What do you love?

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:02.308
-Yeah, I love cherry Jell-O.
-Right.

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:03.843
-Yeah, I love grape Jell-O.

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.844
-What about the lime Jell-O?

00:04:05.844 --> 00:04:07.280
-I'm not a garbage person.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.849
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:16.989
Thank you, regular umbrellas,
for probably looking at

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:18.691
beach umbrellas like,
"Wait, that was

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:21.159
an option this whole time?

00:04:21.159 --> 00:04:22.361
Should've done that."

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:24.330
[ Applause ]

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:31.104
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:34.173
Thank you, sod, for being
Fruit Roll-Ups for dads.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:35.307
There you have it everybody.
-Come on.

00:04:35.307 --> 00:04:36.376
-Those are my thank you notes.

